{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VB1tJSC7P1Kooq5H788KqD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd034-mkdir\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/mkdir: Create Directories\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Build scripts, installers, and deployment pipelines create directory trees as a prerequisite\n6\t  for writing files. The macOS BSD mkdir differs from GNU mkdir in long-option names and\n7\t  fine-grained mode handling with -p. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n8\t  reference binary (gmkdir, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations\n9\t  and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Create one or more directories specified as command-line arguments.\n13\t  - G2: Support recursive creation of intermediate parent directories with -p.\n14\t  - G3: Support explicit permission mode setting with -m.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Basic directory creation\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must create a single directory when invoked as 'mkdir DIR'.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must create multiple directories when invoked with multiple DIR arguments, processing each independently.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target directory already exists and -p is not given.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the parent of the target does not exist and -p is not given.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Parent directory creation (-p, --parents)\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -p or --parents must create intermediate parent directories as needed, similar to 'mkdir -p a/b/c' creating a, a/b, and a/b/c.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must not report an error when the target directory already exists and -p is given.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: Must not report an error when intermediate directories already exist and -p is given.\n38\t\n39\t  R3:\n40\t    title: Mode setting (-m, --mode)\n41\t    items:\n42\t      - R3.1:\n43\t          text: -m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the file permission bits of the created directory to MODE, where MODE is an octal value or symbolic mode string.\n44\t      - R3.2:\n45\t          text: When -m is not given, must create directories with default permissions (0777 modified by the process umask).\n46\t      - R3.3:\n47\t          text: When -p is combined with -m, must apply the specified mode only to the final target directory; intermediate directories must be created with default permissions modified by umask.\n48\t      - R3.4:\n49\t          text: -v or --verbose must print a message to stdout for each directory created.\n50\t\n51\t  R4:\n52\t    title: Differential testing\n53\t    items:\n54\t      - R4.1:\n55\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and gmkdir via pkg/testutils.\n56\t      - R4.2:\n57\t          text: \"Tests must cover: single directory creation, multiple directory creation, -p with nested paths, -p on existing directory, -m with octal mode, -v verbose output, and error cases for missing parents and existing targets.\"\n58\t      - R4.3:\n59\t          text: Tests must verify that permission bits match between the Go implementation and gmkdir for all -m and -p combinations.\n60\t\n61\tnon_goals:\n62\t  - cmd/mkdir does not implement SELinux context options (-Z, --context).\n63\t  - cmd/mkdir does not read directory names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n64\t\n65\tacceptance_criteria:\n66\t  - id: AC1\n67\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir testdir creates a directory named 'testdir', matching gmkdir.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R1.3\n72\t      - R1.4\n73\t  - id: AC2\n74\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir -p a/b/c creates the full directory chain a/b/c, matching gmkdir -p.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.3\n77\t      - R1.4\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.2\n80\t      - R2.3\n81\t      - R3.3\n82\t      - R4.2\n83\t      - R4.3\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir -m 0755 testdir creates a directory with mode 0755, matching gmkdir -m 0755.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R3.1\n88\t      - R3.2\n89\t      - R3.3\n90\t      - R4.2\n91\t      - R4.3\n92\t  - id: AC4\n93\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir existing_dir exits non-zero with an error message when existing_dir already exists, matching gmkdir.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R1.3\n96\t      - R1.4\n97\t      - R2.2\n98\t      - R2.3\n99\t      - R4.1\n100\t      - R4.2\n101\t  - id: AC5\n102\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gmkdir passes for single creation, multiple creation, -p, -m, -v, and error cases.\"\n103\t    traces:\n104\t      - R1.3\n105\t      - R1.4\n106\t      - R2.1\n107\t      - R2.2\n108\t      - R2.3\n109\t      - R3.1\n110\t      - R3.2\n111\t      - R3.3\n112\t      - R3.4\n113\t      - R4.1\n114\t      - R4.2\n115\t      - R4.3\n116\t  - id: AC6\n117\t    criterion: \"cmd/mkdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n118\t    traces:\n119\t      - R1.1\n120\t      - R1.2\n121\t      - R1.3\n122\t      - R1.4\n123\t      - R2.1\n124\t      - R2.2\n125\t      - R2.3\n126\t      - R3.1\n127\t      - R3.2\n128\t      - R3.3\n129\t      - R3.4\n130\t      - R4.1\n131\t      - R4.2\n132\t      - R4.3\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31ef50e3-681a-4137-95d4-8d627c434c8f","uuid":"e8658691-79f3-43fb-823f-82b576dff1cf","timestamp":"2026-05-20T00:17:36.023Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5325/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd034-mkdir.yaml","content":"id: srd034-mkdir\ntitle: \"cmd/mkdir: Create Directories\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Build scripts, installers, and deployment pipelines create directory trees as a prerequisite\n  for writing files. The macOS BSD mkdir differs from GNU mkdir in long-option names and\n  fine-grained mode handling with -p. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (gmkdir, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations\n  and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create one or more directories specified as command-line arguments.\n  - G2: Support recursive creation of intermediate parent directories with -p.\n  - G3: Support explicit permission mode setting with -m.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic directory creation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must create a single directory when invoked as 'mkdir DIR'.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must create multiple directories when invoked with multiple DIR arguments, processing each independently.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target directory already exists and -p is not given.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the parent of the target does not exist and -p is not given.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Parent directory creation (-p, --parents)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -p or --parents must create intermediate parent directories as needed, similar to 'mkdir -p a/b/c' creating a, a/b, and a/b/c.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must not report an error when the target directory already exists and -p is given.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must not report an error when intermediate directories already exist and -p is given.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Mode setting (-m, --mode)\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the file permission bits of the created directory to MODE, where MODE is an octal value or symbolic mode string.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: When -m is not given, must create directories with default permissions (0777 modified by the process umask).\n      - R3.3:\n          text: When -p is combined with -m, must apply the specified mode only to the final target directory; intermediate directories must be created with default permissions modified by umask.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: -v or --verbose must print a message to stdout for each directory created.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and gmkdir via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: single directory creation, multiple directory creation, -p with nested paths, -p on existing directory, -m with octal mode, -v verbose output, and error cases for missing parents and existing targets.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that permission bits match between the Go implementation and gmkdir for all -m and -p combinations.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/mkdir does not implement SELinux context options (-Z, --context).\n  - cmd/mkdir does not read directory names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir testdir creates a directory named 'testdir', matching gmkdir.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir -p a/b/c creates the full directory chain a/b/c, matching gmkdir -p.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir -m 0755 testdir creates a directory with mode 0755, matching gmkdir -m 0755.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mkdir existing_dir exits non-zero with an error message when existing_dir already exists, matching gmkdir.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gmkdir passes for single creation, multiple creation, -p, -m, -v, and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/mkdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
