{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5325) that requires implementing parent directory creation support (`-p`/`--parents` flag) for `cmd/mkdir`. The specific requirements from srd034-mkdir are:\n   - R2.1: `-p` or `--parents` must create intermediate parent directories as needed (e.g., `mkdir -p a/b/c` creates a, a/b, and a/b/c)\n   - R2.2: Must not report an error when the target directory already exists and `-p` is given\n   - R2.3: Must not report an error when intermediate directories already exist and `-p` is given\n   \n   Acceptance criteria require: compilation without errors, `go vet` passes, all tests pass (existing + new `-p` tests against `gmkdir` reference binary), and `-p` correctly creates intermediate dirs without erroring on existing ones.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (`gmkdir`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - `os.MkdirAll` for recursive directory creation (Go stdlib equivalent of `mkdir -p`)\n   - `os.Mkdir` for single directory creation (existing basic behavior)\n   - Custom argument parsing (no cobra/flag - hand-rolled arg parsing)\n   - Error message normalization via regex to strip binary path differences\n   - The execution constitution mandates: no git commands, write-all-then-build strategy, 40-line function limit, copyright headers, no scope creep\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd034-mkdir.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for mkdir requirements. R2 group (parent directory creation) is the focus of this task.\n     - Key requirements: R2.1 (create intermediates), R2.2 (no error on existing target with -p), R2.3 (no error on existing intermediates with -p)\n     - Non-goals: SELinux context options (-Z, --context)\n\n   - **cmd/mkdir/main.go** (to be modified)\n     - Existing implementation covers R1.1-R1.4 (basic directory creation)\n     - Current `options` struct has only `verbose bool` - needs `parents bool` added\n     - `run` function uses `os.Mkdir(dir, 0o777)` - needs conditional `os.MkdirAll` path for `-p`\n     - `parseShortFlags` handles only `'v'` - needs `'p'` added\n     - `parseLongFlag` handles `--help`, `--version`, `--verbose` - needs `--parents` added\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd034-mkdir R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: mkdir [OPTION]... DIRECTORY...\n     Create the DIRECTORY(ies), if they do not already exist.\n     \n     Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.\n       -m, --mode=MODE   set file mode (as in chmod), not a=rwx - umask\n       -p, --parents     no error if existing, make parent directories as needed,\n                         with their file modes unaffected by any -m option\n       -v, --verbose     print a message for each created directory\n       -Z                set SELinux security context of each created directory\n                         to the default type\n           --context[=CTX]  like -Z, or if CTX is specified then set the\n                         SELinux or SMACK security context to CTX\n           --help        display this help and exit\n           --version     output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `mkdir (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     type options struct {\n         verbose bool\n     }\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, dirs, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"mkdir: %s\\n\", err)\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'mkdir --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         os.Exit(run(opts, dirs))\n     }\n     \n     func run(opts options, dirs []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, dir := range dirs {\n             if err := os.Mkdir(dir, 0o777); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"mkdir: cannot create directory '%s': %s\\n\",\n                     dir, sysErrMsg(err))\n                 exitCode = 1\n                 continue\n             }\n             if opts.verbose {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mkdir: created directory '%s'\\n\", dir)\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func sysErrMsg(err error) string {\n         pe, ok := err.(*os.PathError)\n         if !ok { return err.Error() }\n         se, ok := pe.Err.(syscall.Errno)\n         if !ok { return pe.Err.Error() }\n         switch se {\n         case syscall.EEXIST: return \"File exists\"\n         case syscall.ENOENT: return \"No such file or directory\"\n         case syscall.EACCES: return \"Permission denied\"\n         case syscall.ENOTDIR: return \"Not a directory\"\n         default: return se.Error()\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n         var opts options\n         var dirs []string\n         i := 0\n         for i < len(args) {\n             arg := args[i]\n             if arg == \"--\" { dirs = append(dirs, args[i+1:]...); break }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n                 n, err := parseLongFlag(arg, &opts)\n                 if err != nil { return opts, nil, err }\n                 i += n; continue\n             }\n             if len(arg) > 1 && arg[0] == '-' {\n                 if err := parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts); err != nil { return opts, nil, err }\n                 i++; continue\n             }\n             dirs = append(dirs, arg); i++\n         }\n         if len(dirs) == 0 { return opts, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing operand\") }\n         return opts, dirs, nil\n     }\n     \n     func parseLongFlag(flag string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n         switch flag {\n         case \"--help\": fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText); os.Exit(0); return 0, nil\n         case \"--version\": fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText); os.Exit(0); return 0, nil\n         case \"--verbose\": opts.verbose = true; return 1, nil\n         default: return 0, fmt.Errorf(\"unrecognized option '%s'\", flag)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) error {\n         for j := 0; j < len(flags); j++ {\n             switch flags[j] {\n             case 'v': opts.verbose = true\n             default: return fmt.Errorf(\"invalid option -- '%c'\", flags[j])\n             }\n         }\n         return nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go** (to be modified)\n     - Existing tests cover R1 and R4 (basic creation + differential testing)\n     - Uses custom `runBin` and `compareResults` helpers (not RunDiffTests for creation tests since they need separate temp dirs)\n     - Uses `runCreationTest` helper for tests that create directories\n     - Has `normalizeBinaryName` regex to normalize `gmkdir`/`mkdir` path differences\n     - Full existing test code included above (231 lines)\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (reference only - DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests)\n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (reference only - InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Work was interrupted at the reading/planning phase before any code was written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully read all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file)\n   - Identified what changes are needed: add `parents bool` to options, add `-p`/`--parents` parsing, add conditional `os.MkdirAll` logic in `run`, and add `-p` tests\n   - Key consideration: When `-p` is used with `-v` (verbose), need to print messages for each directory created including intermediates. GNU mkdir with `-p -v` prints a line for each intermediate directory created. This may require custom implementation rather than just `os.MkdirAll`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The entire stitch task prompt with full project context, SRD specifications, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, and all project documentation inline. This is the task assignment for implementing srd034 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 (mkdir -p parent directory creation).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `-p`/`--parents` flag in `cmd/mkdir/main.go`:\n     - Add `parents bool` to `options` struct\n     - Add `'p'` case to `parseShortFlags`\n     - Add `\"--parents\"` case to `parseLongFlag`\n     - Modify `run` function to handle `-p` (use `os.MkdirAll` or custom logic for verbose+parents)\n   - Add differential tests in `cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go`:\n     - Test `-p` with nested path creation (`a/b/c`)\n     - Test `-p` on existing directory (should succeed silently)\n     - Test `-p` with some intermediate dirs already existing\n     - Test `-p` with verbose output\n     - Test `-p` with multiple arguments\n   - Run `go build -o bin/mkdir ./cmd/mkdir/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/mkdir/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/mkdir/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (srd034-mkdir.yaml, cmd/mkdir/main.go, cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go) and was about to plan the implementation approach and write code. The task description states: \"Add -p flag support for creating parent directories\" to main.go and \"Add differential tests for -p parent creation behavior\" to the test file. The implementation needs to handle:\n   - `os.MkdirAll` for creating parent directories when `-p` is given\n   - Suppressing errors when target or intermediates already exist with `-p`\n   - Verbose output with `-p` needs to print each intermediate directory created (this requires walking the path to determine which dirs are new, since `os.MkdirAll` doesn't report what it created)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/mkdir/main.go` with `-p`/`--parents` support added. Specifically:\n   - Add `parents bool` to the `options` struct\n   - Add `'p'` to `parseShortFlags` and `\"--parents\"` to `parseLongFlag`\n   - Create a `createWithParents` function for the `-p` path in `run` that uses `os.MkdirAll` and handles verbose output for intermediate dirs\n   - Then write the modified test file with new `-p` test cases\n   - Then build and test\n\n   The task description says: \"Implement srd034 R2.1 as specified in the SRD -- add the -p / --parents flag that creates intermediate parent directories as needed\", \"Implement srd034 R2.2 as specified in the SRD -- when -p is given and the target directory already exists, do not report an error\", \"Implement srd034 R2.3 as specified in the SRD -- handle -p interaction with other flags and multi-argument invocations\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5325/31ef50e3-681a-4137-95d4-8d627c434c8f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":n